        "id": "PRRC_kwDOKStajs733aZn",
        "database_id": 4158498407,
        "body": "Agree, enum is cleaner. Since it is not blocker, and the scope of the changes to do clean changes are big (see below), how about let's do it at subsequent PR? I filed issue #4732 to track it.\r\n\r\nMore details:\r\nthe two parameters are declared as `bool aligned, bool dma` in main's `view.hpp`, `views.hpp` and `expr.hpp`. An `enum class` value does not convert to `bool`. So the enum change must edit those three headers, plus `slice.hpp`, `tensor.hpp`, `dotter.hpp` and the five `static constexpr bool dma` members. It must also rewrite the 80 existing call sites (82 lines in 20 files) that pass bare `true, false`. \r\n\r\nYour #4697 keeps `bool Dma` in its new aliases. So the enum change should land after #4697. I am taking #4697 into this branch first.",
        "created_at": "2026-10-01T17:36:31Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-10-01T17:36:32Z",
        "author": {
