        "body": "`native_k_view` is an alias of the generic row-major `view`, and t_llama_unit asserts it is constructible from `const bf16*`. So any pointer or row-major 64x128 bf16 view passes the QK kernel; \"a bare pointer is a compile error\" holds for V only. Fine as a first step, but please say so in the description and give K a distinct type in #4424.",
